":"Consult your healthcare practitioner prior to use."},{"type":"Precautions re: Pregnant or Nursing or Prescription Medications","notes":"Individuals taking medication should discuss potential interactions with their healthcare practitioner."},{"type":"Precautions re: All Other","notes":"Do not use if tamper seal is damaged."},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"XYMOGEN's Methylcobalamin provides 5 mg (5,000 mcg) of vitamin B12 in each very small, pleasant-tasting tablet. Methylcobalamin, the form of B12 active in the body, appears to be better absorbed and stored in tissues in comparison to cyanocobalamin. Methylcobalamin has multiple supportive roles in the body, including red blood cell formation, nervous system health, homocysteine and folate metabolism, melatonin synthesis, and more."},{"type":"FDA Disclaimer Statement","notes":"These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease."},{"type":"Storage","notes":"Storage: Keep closed in a cool, dry place out of reach of children."},{"type":"Precautions re: Children","notes":"Storage: Keep closed in a cool, dry place out of reach of children."},{"type":"Formulation re: Does NOT Contain","notes":"Does not contain: Wheat, gluten, yeast, soy, animal or dairy products, fish, shellfish, peanuts, tree nuts, egg, ingredients derived from genetically modified organisms (GMOs), artificial colors, artificial sweeteners, or artificial preservatives."},{"type":"Formula re: Contains","notes":"Methyl B12"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"ePV:"},{"type":"FDA Statement of Identity","notes":"Dietary Supplement"},{"type":"Seals/Symbols","notes":"ePV (ePedigree Verification)"},{"type":"General Statements: All Other Content","notes":"Exclusive professional formulas"},{"type":"Brand IP Statement(s) re: (c), (TM), (SM)","notes":"Copyright 2019 XYMOGEN"},{"type":"Seals/Symbols","notes":"GMP Complaint Verifi